we're joined by  aidan mclaughlin the editor-in-chief of  media which like the law and crime trial  network is part of the abrams media  group in aiden we begin with your choice  for the winner which surprised me the  cnn new year's eve team of anderson  cooper and an apparently quite  inebriated andy cohen who delivered a  belittling farewell to outgoing mayor  of new york city bill de blasio  after four years  as the mayor of new york  the only thing  that democrats and republicans can agree  on  is what a horrible  mayor has been  so  sayonara sucka  wow 2022.  i mean it's a new year  all right aidan tell us why that was a  media winner  so just for the record andy cohen has  been defending himself he said that he's  not going to apologize for getting a  little uh inebriated on new year's eve  which i think is a sentiment we can all  uh agree with uh the reason that they  were named winner is just because of the  rating um cnn's new year's eve special  which took place in times square it was  the most watched event on cable news in  america uh in 2022. um so it started at  8 p.m it ran over five hours just the  portion with andy cohen and anderson  cooper and it averaged 2.12 million  viewers over the course of that time uh  in the demo which as you know brian is  the sort of advertiser coveted age  demographic they drew almost 800 000  viewers which is really a staggering  amount for cable news right now  particularly at that hour it's also a  huge amount for cnn and was cnn's most  watch event in month um it also meant  that the network beat out fox news uh  and msnbc in the ratings for the show  which is a big deal because the network  has had a pretty rocky 2021 in the  ratings  it beat fox news in january for the  first time in years but then sunk down  to third place for the rest of the year  as fox news surged back uh to first um  so the show had plenty of highlights um  you know a little bit of controversy but  ultimately really good ratings and  that's why they were winner  this is the road to success for jeff  zucker now and his cnn ratings issues  you know i think it's a typical cnn  rating story uh when they have big  events like this that are sort of must  watch everyone turns to cnn they have  that with breaking news that's why  january they had such high ratings it  was because of the end of the trump  administration and the riot at the  capitol um when you go down to weeks  that do not have big events or big news  cycles cnn drops the third behind fox  news and msnbc um but it's really for  big events like these that everyone  tuned to cnn and jeff sucker's really  good at making those shows happen  well that was quite a show to watch  that's for sure now let's turn to this  week's loser sean hannity at fox news  why sean hannity aiden  that's right so the house select  committee which is investigating the  january 6 riot at the capitol published  a letter that they sent to the fox news  host requesting his cooperation in their  investigation  now the committee says they're in  possession of thousands of documents uh  including a trove of information uh that  was given to them by former trump chief  of staff mark meadows now in that trove  of documents are texts that sean hannity  sent to mark meadows around january 6  and they published a few of those in  that new letter  one of them uh was sean handy warning  the trump administration that things  could get ugly right before january 6.  another one said that was which was sent  after january 6 urged the trump  administration to not mention the  election ever again now what's so  stunning about this message is that it  displays on the part of sean hannity a  real understanding that trump's lies  about the 2020 election are dangerous  and directly resulted in the riot at the  capitol and i suppose you have to give  him credit for that on the other hand  what's disappointing is that in the  years since on air sean hannity has  declined to tell his viewers that their  trump bears any responsibility for the  violence that happened that day and in  fact has continued to propagate this  idea that there were um you know uh  problems with the last election um and  that it should be looked at and that  trump was hard done by by it so you know  sean hannity revealing in private that  he had concerns about what was happening  that day going on air and not saying  that there was any connection between  the riot and president donald trump um  that's a real problem for him and so  quickly in 15 seconds what about the  first amendment issue here of congress  trying to get testimony from a reporter  well i think that's an issue as well and  that's certainly how sean hannity is  going to fight it so far he has not  commented publicly about this neither  has fox news they have not responded to  any of our requests for comment um so  we'll see how what their strategy is  going to be to combat this but i have a  feeling he's going to cooperate at the  end of the day all right aidan  mclaughlin the editor in chief of media  thank you very much for being here and  welcome to our program for the year and  that is our program for tonight thanks  for joining us we'll see you back here  next week on the law on crime trial  network  [Music]  do  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

